    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's review the scene line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Шеф, я сделал это.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, I did it.' The verb for 'did' is in the masculine past tense, marked by that 'l' sound at the end.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Что ты сделал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What did you make?' The verb for 'did' is in the masculine past tense, marked by that 'l' sound at the end.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Я сделал ваш паштет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I made your pâté.' Maks starts with 'I' and pairs it with 'did' to make the point clear. And Chef jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Мой паштет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My pâté?' Chef puts 'pâté' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'pâté'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Получилось один в один.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It came out exactly the same.' The key word here means 'worked out', which Maks combines with 'one'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Я должен попробовать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I must taste it.' Chef puts 'I' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'has to'. Maks answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Даже чуть-чуть лучше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Even a little better.' Maks puts 'a little bit' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'better'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Да ладно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No way!' The first content word means 'yes', and 'all right' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Да.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yeah.' You'll hear 'yes' all the time in the show, here connected with 'yes'. Then Chef replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Это невозможно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is impossible.' A compact expression built around 'this' and 'impossible'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Я хороший повар.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am a good cook.' Listen for the word meaning 'I' right alongside 'good' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Мы посмотрим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We will see.' The first content word means 'we', and 'have a look' rounds out the thought. Let's listen to the dialog one more time.",
      "gap": 0.9
